---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SourceAvailabilityNotice from '../components/SourceAvailabilityNotice.astro';
import config from '../../site.config.json';
import { records, sources, unavailableSources, stats, generatedAt, dataLastmod, fmtDate } from '../lib/data.js';

const origin = config.SITE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const datasetModified = ['2026-09-24', dataLastmod].filter(Boolean).sort().at(-1);
const earliestObservation = records
  .flatMap(record => record.history.map(observation => observation.effective_date))
  .filter(Boolean)
  .sort()
  .at(0);
const downloads = [
  {
    name: 'Current routes',
    path: '/api/v1/downloads/latest.csv',
    rows: stats.entities,
    description: 'One row per retained route, including source collection status and last successful verification.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Append-only history',
    path: '/api/v1/downloads/history.csv',
    rows: stats.observations,
    description: 'Every distinct public observation, with route context and source dates.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Forward-looking projections',
    path: '/api/v1/downloads/forward-looking.csv',
    rows: stats.forward_looking_estimates,
    description: 'IRCC current projections and application-month cohort rows.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Source register',
    path: '/api/v1/downloads/sources.csv',
    rows: sources.length,
    description: 'Primary-source URLs, agencies and source-specific reuse notes.',
  },
];
const jsonld = [{
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  '@id': `${origin}/data/#dataset`,
  name: 'GovWait government processing-time dataset',
  description: 'Officially published government processing and wait times for visas, permits, sponsorships, resettlement and passports, with per-value provenance and append-only history.',
  url: `${origin}/data/`,
  identifier: `${origin}/data/#dataset`,
  datePublished: '2026-08-21',
  dateModified: datasetModified,
  temporalCoverage: `${earliestObservation}/..`,
  spatialCoverage: ['Canada', 'United Kingdom', 'New Zealand', 'Norway'],
  isAccessibleForFree: true,
  creator: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    '@id': `${origin}/#organization`,
    name: config.SITE_NAME,
    url: origin,
  },
  publisher: { '@id': `${origin}/#organization` },
  license: `${origin}/data-license/`,
  keywords: [
    'government processing times', 'visa processing times', 'immigration data',
    'permit wait times', 'IRCC', 'UKVI', 'Immigration New Zealand', 'UDI',
  ],
  variableMeasured: [
    'official published wait value', 'normalized duration in days', 'publication or first-observed date',
    'retrieval timestamp', 'source URL', 'availability status',
  ],
  isBasedOn: [...new Set(sources.map(source => source.url))],
  distribution: downloads.map(download => ({
    '@type': 'DataDownload',
    name: `${download.name} CSV`,
    description: download.description,
    encodingFormat: 'text/csv',
    contentUrl: `${origin}${download.path}`,
  })),
}];
---
<Base title="Government processing-time dataset — free CSV downloads | GovWait"
      description="Download GovWait's source-backed government processing-time dataset as CSV, including latest retained routes, source status, append-only history, IRCC projections and provenance."
      jsonld={jsonld}>
  <nav class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> › Data</nav>
  <h1>Government processing-time dataset</h1>
  <p class="lede">Free, source-backed data for {stats.entities.toLocaleString()} processing-time routes across {stats.jurisdictions.length} governments. Download latest retained values, append-only history, IRCC forward-looking projections and the complete source register—no account or API key required.</p>

  <div class="stats">
    <div><div class="n">{stats.entities.toLocaleString()}</div><div class="l">routes retained</div></div>
    <div><div class="n">{stats.observations.toLocaleString()}</div><div class="l">recorded observations</div></div>
    <div><div class="n">{stats.forward_looking_estimates.toLocaleString()}</div><div class="l">projection rows</div></div>
    <div><div class="n">{sources.length}</div><div class="l">official sources</div></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Download the data</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Rows</th><th>What it contains</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {downloads.map(download => (
        <tr>
          <td><a href={download.path} download>{download.name} (.csv)</a></td>
          <td class="num">{download.rows.toLocaleString()}</td>
          <td>{download.description}</td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p class="small">Prefer JSON? Start with the <a href="/api/v1/index.json">API index</a> or <a href="/api-docs/">API documentation</a>. Machines can read the <a href="/api/v1/dataset.json">dataset metadata document</a>.</p>

  <h2>Why this dataset is different</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Every value points to a primary government source.</strong> Route records preserve the official URL and retrieval timestamp.</li>
    <li><strong>History is append-only.</strong> New observations are added; earlier published values are not silently replaced.</li>
    <li><strong>Dates mean what they say.</strong> We use the agency's own update date when supplied. When a source has no date, a changed value receives a clearly described first-observed date.</li>
    <li><strong>Different measures stay separate.</strong> Backward-looking times, forward projections, service standards and percentile measures carry distinct <code>metric_type</code> values.</li>
    <li><strong>Missing answers remain honest.</strong> <code>unavailable</code> and <code>insufficient_data</code> are published states, not estimates.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Core fields</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>entity_id</code></td><td>Stable route-and-metric identifier used by the JSON API.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>value_raw</code></td><td>The official published wording, preserved as displayed by the source.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>value_days</code></td><td>Normalized comparison value. The original unit remains in <code>unit_original</code>; range values use the upper end conservatively.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>metric_type</code></td><td>Whether the figure is published, backward-looking, forward-looking, a service standard or a percentile.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>effective_date</code></td><td>Agency update date when available; otherwise the first date GovWait observed that value.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>retrieved_at</code></td><td>UTC timestamp when GovWait fetched the source.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>source_url</code></td><td>Official government page or data file for the observation.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>source_collection_status</code></td><td><code>active</code> when scheduled collection is available, or <code>source_unavailable</code> when GovWait has stopped fetching and is preserving the last verified snapshot.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>source_last_verified_at</code></td><td>The last successful GovWait source verification. It does not advance during a source outage or access closure.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2>Freshness and method</h2>
  <p>The current export was generated {fmtDate(generatedAt)}. The newest official update or first-observed date represented is {fmtDate(dataLastmod)}. GovWait checks active sources on a regular schedule, but each agency publishes on its own cadence. A failed active source or validation check stops publication rather than producing a guessed value; a source formally removed from collection remains clearly labeled with its last successful verification.</p>
  {unavailableSources.map(source => <SourceAvailabilityNotice source={source} />)}
  <p>Read the full <a href="/about/">collection method and source register</a>, the <a href="/about/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>, and the <a href="/data-license/">data reuse and licensing notice</a>.</p>

  <h2>Suggested citation</h2>
  <pre class="code"><code>GovWait. “GovWait government processing-time dataset.” Version 1, https://govwait.com/data/. Accessed [date].</code></pre>
  <p class="small muted">GovWait is independent and is not affiliated with any government. The data is reference information, not legal or immigration advice, and no published time predicts an individual case.</p>
</Base>
